  "articleBody": {
    "tokens": "CSS variables land by default in v6, which finally makes a live theme editor practical rather than theoretical.",
    "cjk": "Latin line-heights crush 汉字, and negative tracking makes them worse. Two parallel type scales fix it.",
    "datatable": "antd's Table already owns rendering. What it lacks is a toolbar, column control and a safe export.",
    "bundle": "MSW is a mock server. It has no business in a production build, and its dependency tree is larger than it looks.",
    "msw": "One set of handlers serving the dev server, the test runner and the public demo keeps them from drifting apart.",
    "darkmode": "Three states, not two: explicit light, explicit dark, and the far more common unstamped system default.",
    "vite8": "Rolldown does the React transform through Oxc, so the SWC plugin is now the slower path."
